{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"artless-sweaty-bear","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAn `s3://` ticket-store remote is only safe with a `git-remote-s3` helper that has the\n`IfNoneMatch` per-ref lock: a live experiment this session proved that a client **without**\nthat lock is exactly what leaves two `<sha>.bundle` files for one ref, producing the\nmultiple-bundles corruption that makes the store unclonable. Today nothing stops rebar from\ndriving an `s3://` remote with a missing or too-old helper — the failure would surface later\nas silent store corruption rather than at the point of misconfiguration.\n\nThe sibling story (\"Declare the optional [s3] extra…\") provides `require_s3_helper()` in\n`src/rebar/_optional.py`, which confirms the helper is on `PATH` and `>=0.3.2`. This story\n**wires that guard in** so any store operation targeting an `s3://` remote fails closed early\nwith an actionable message.\n\n## Approach\n\nDetect \"S3 mode\" by the **remote URL scheme** — no new config key (reuse the existing\n`sync.remote`, `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` `SyncConfig.remote`). Resolve the configured\nremote's URL with `git remote get-url <sync.remote>` (via the existing shell-out layer\n`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` `run_git`) and treat it as S3 mode iff it starts with `s3://`\n(git-remote-s3's own scheme; also accept `s3+zip://`).\n\nAdd one small internal preflight — `_require_s3_helper_if_s3_remote(base_path)` — that\nresolves the remote URL, and when it is an `s3://` URL calls\n`rebar._optional.require_s3_helper()`, letting its actionable error propagate. Call it:\n\n- at the **start of `push_tickets_branch`** (`src/rebar/_store/push.py:168`), before the\n  first push attempt, so every auto-push is gated; and\n- during **store init/mount** in `src/rebar/_commands/init.py` (where the tracker worktree\n  and remote are first established), so misconfiguration is caught at setup, not first write.\n\nWhen the remote URL is not `s3://` (the default GitHub case) the preflight is a no-op — the\nexisting code path is completely unchanged.\n\nRationale: keying off the URL scheme reuses the field git-remote-s3 already keys off,\nrequires zero schema/migration work, and keeps the blast radius to `s3://` remotes only;\nplacing the check at both init and push gives a fail-fast at configuration time plus a\nbelt-and-suspenders guard on the hot write path, both funneling through the single tested\n`require_s3_helper()` seam.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py` — add the preflight call at the top of `push_tickets_branch`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/init.py` — call the preflight during init/mount.\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` — (only if not already trivially available) a tiny\n  `resolve_remote_url(base_path, remote)` helper wrapping `git remote get-url`.\n- `tests/` — CLI/subprocess tests for the fail-closed behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **CLI subprocess** against a real temporary git repo configured with an `s3://`\n`sync.remote` (no AWS calls needed — the guard fails before any network I/O). Oracles:\n- Failure (helper missing): with `git-remote-s3` not on `PATH`, `rebar init`/a push path\n  against an `s3://` remote exits non-zero and prints the message naming `pip install '.[s3]'`.\n- Edge (helper too old): monkeypatch the version probe to `0.2.9` → same fail-closed message\n  naming the `>=0.3.2` minimum.\n- Happy / no-regression (non-S3 remote): with a `file://` or GitHub-style remote, the\n  preflight is a no-op and init/push behave exactly as before even with no helper installed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With `sync.remote` pointing at an `s3://` URL and the helper absent, store init and the\n      push path both **exit non-zero** with a single actionable message naming\n      `pip install '.[s3]'`. Verified by the CLI subprocess failure oracle.\n- [ ] With the helper present but below `0.3.2`, the same paths fail closed naming the\n      `>=0.3.2` minimum. Verified by the too-old edge oracle.\n- [ ] With a non-`s3://` `sync.remote`, the preflight is a no-op: init and push succeed with\n      no helper installed and no behavior change. Verified by the no-regression oracle.\n- [ ] S3 mode is detected purely from the remote URL scheme (no new config key added).\n      Verified by inspection and by the config schema being unchanged in this story.","id":"8970-40af-1785-4530","parent_id":"cf3c-1444-863e-49d7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Fail closed when an s3:// ticket remote is used without a locking git-remote-s3 helper"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786149311176458001,"uuid":"698210c7-3f2f-483c-8001-a58d7b2fe1b5"}